markdown <<MARKDOWN
# Types of Loops

#### Not all loops repeat in the same way. What makes loops different is how the repetition is controlled.

#### In most programs, iteration falls into one of two common categories.

<div style="
  display: flex;
  gap: 20px;
  justify-content: center;
  align-items: stretch;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
">

  <!-- Count-Controlled Iteration Card -->
  <div style="
    background-color: #F5F7F8;
    color: #000000;
    padding: 20px;
    border-radius: 10px;
    box-shadow: 2px 2px 8px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
    width: 300px;
    text-align: left;
  ">

<p style="font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold; margin: 0; ">
      Count-Controlled Iteration<br>(For Loop)
    </p>

<ul style="
  list-style-position: outside; padding-left: 16px; margin: 12px 0 0 0;">


<li style="font-size: 13pt; line-height: 1.3; margin-bottom: 8px; margin-left: 0;  padding-left: 0;
">
        Repeats a set of steps a <strong>specific number of times</strong>
      </li>

<li style="  font-size: 13pt; line-height: 1.3; margin-bottom: 8px; margin-left: 0;padding-left: 0;">
        The number of repetitions is known before the loop starts
      </li>

 <li style="  font-size: 13pt; line-height: 1.3; margin-bottom: 8px; margin-left: 0;padding-left: 0; font-style: italic;">
         “How many times should this happen?”
      </li>

 </ul>

  </div>

  <!-- Condition-Controlled Iteration Card -->
  <div style="
    background-color: #F5F7F8;
    color: #000000;
    padding: 20px;
    border-radius: 10px;
    box-shadow: 2px 2px 8px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
    width: 300px;
    text-align: left;
  ">

 <p style="font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold; margin: 0;">
      Condition-Controlled Iteration<br>(While Loop)
    </p>

<ul style="
  list-style-position: outside; padding-left: 16px; margin: 12px 0 0 0;">

<li style="  font-size: 13pt; line-height: 1.3; margin-bottom: 8px; margin-left: 0;padding-left: 0;">
        Repeats a set of steps <strong>as long as a condition is true</strong>
      </li>

 <li style="  font-size: 13pt; line-height: 1.3; margin-bottom: 8px; margin-left: 0;padding-left: 0;">
        The number of repetitions is not known ahead of time
      </li>

 <li style="  font-size: 13pt; line-height: 1.3; margin-bottom: 8px; margin-left: 0;padding-left: 0; font-style: italic;">
         “When should this stop?”
      </li>

</ul>

  </div>

</div>

## Let's look at the flow charts
#### Below are two flowcharts that show iteration in action.
#### Before labeling them, take a moment to study how each one repeats.
---


## Flowchart A

<img src="https://images.code.org/d80a0b774a89fa285465c1a50a654d79-image-1768419690819.png" alt="flowchart for a for loop" width="350px" style="border-radius:10px; float:left; margin: 0px 30px 30px 40px;">

#### **Think about:**

- #### What causes the steps to repeat?

- #### Is the number of repetitions fixed?

- #### What makes the loop stop?

 #### 👉 **Which type of loop do you think this represents?**



<div style="clear:both;"></div>



<details style="background-color: #ececec; padding: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; border: 1px solid transparent; border-radius: 5px;">
    <summary style="font-size: 1.5em; font-weight: bold;">💡 Check your thinking:</summary>
<div style="margin-top: 20px; margin-left: 20px; margin-right: 20px; margin-bottom:75px;">
    <p style = "font-size: 14pt;">
  Flowchart A represents a <b>count-controlled loop (for loop) </b> because the number of repetitions is determined in advance.
</p>
</div>
</details>


---

## Flowchart B

<img src="https://images.code.org/4afcb2bde4184c0c4735dcfb18d4a4a2-image-1768418982827.png" alt="flowchart for a while" width="350px" style="border-radius:10px; float:left; margin: 0px 30px 30px 40px;">

#### **Think about:**

- #### Does the loop repeat a known number of times?

- #### Is the number of repetitions fixed?

- #### Or does it continue until a condition changes?

 #### 👉 **Which type of loop do you think this represents?**



<div style="clear:both;"></div>



<details style="background-color: #ececec; padding: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; border: 1px solid transparent; border-radius: 5px;">
    <summary style="font-size: 1.5em; font-weight: bold;">💡 Check your thinking:</summary>
<div style="margin-top: 20px; margin-left: 20px; margin-right: 20px; margin-bottom:75px;">
    <p style = "font-size: 14pt;">
    Flowchart B represents a <b>condition-controlled loop (while loop) </b> because the steps repeat as long as a condition remains true.
</p>
</div>
</details>


## Next up

#### Let's see what this looks like in code starting with for loops. 

